
This blog provides a beginner-friendly introduction to Data Preprocessing, one of the most important stages in the Machine Learning pipeline. It explains how raw data is transformed into a clean and machine-learning-ready format through techniques such as missing value handling, outlier detection, feature scaling, feature transformation, and categorical data encoding.
Topics Covered
Numerical Data Preprocessing
Missing Value Treatment
Outlier Detection and Handling
Feature Scaling (MinMax, Standard, Robust Scaling)
Feature Transformation (Log, Square Root, Reciprocal, Box-Cox, Yeo-Johnson)
Categorical Data Preprocessing
One-Hot Encoding and Ordinal Encoding
Real-World Preprocessing Workflow
Key Learning Outcomes
Understand the importance of preprocessing in machine learning
Learn how to prepare numerical and categorical data for modeling
Explore common scaling and transformation techniques
Build a strong foundation for feature engineering and model development

